\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Retention capacity ($R$) versus porosity ($\varepsilon $) across packing media. The relationship is non-monotonic: materials with similar or higher porosity can exhibit substantially lower retention depending on hydraulic and frictional signatures. Glass marbles exhibit low retention despite moderate porosity relative to other media, visually demonstrating the porosity paradox.}}{7}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:retention_vs_porosity}{{1}{7}{Retention capacity ($R$) versus porosity ($\varepsilon $) across packing media. The relationship is non-monotonic: materials with similar or higher porosity can exhibit substantially lower retention depending on hydraulic and frictional signatures. Glass marbles exhibit low retention despite moderate porosity relative to other media, visually demonstrating the porosity paradox}{figure.1}{}}
